From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: GL: the vertex stages' depth_scale and depth_offset renamed

azahar-nano gave the vertex stages' vs_data block depth_scale and
depth_offset; fs_data has members by the same names. Neither block has an
instance name, so in GLSL ES their members share one namespace across the
program, and Mali refused to link every program: "Shaders use a uniform block
with no instance object vs_data that conflicts with the member of the uniform
block fs_data which have no instance object." No draw reached the screen.

Vulkan compiles each stage to SPIR-V on its own (no clash) and keys its VS
SPIR-V cache by the generated text, so the generator is left alone and only
the GL backend renames the two (vs_depth_scale, vs_depth_offset) in the vertex
and geometry stages it builds: the programmable and trivial vertex shaders,
the fixed geometry shader and the disk cache's rebuild. The block is bound by
its binding, so the names never reach the C++ side.

